---
layout: layouts/base.njk
bodyClass: page-home
faqs:
  - q: "Do all our members need smartphones?"
    a: "No. Branch staff record cash, transfers and POS payments for every member in Coop Staff. Members who have a smartphone can also use Coop Member to check their balances, apply for loans and pay in. It works on Android, iPhone and in any web browser."
  - q: "When members pay online, where does the money go?"
    a: "Straight into your society’s own bank account, which we confirm first. Payments go through Paystack, a Nigerian payment company. CoopCircle never holds your money. Members see the small payment fee before they pay."
  - q: "Can we bring in our existing records?"
    a: "Yes. On Growth and above, you can upload your members and their balances from an Excel file. Another leader checks and confirms the upload before it counts. You can undo an upload for 7 days."
  - q: "What happens to our data if we stop using CoopCircle?"
    a: "Your data belongs to you. On every plan, even Free, your leaders can download all of your society’s data. Every member can also download their own."
  - q: "Does it work for a society with branches?"
    a: "Yes. Each branch records its own payments and hands in the cash it collects. Leaders can see all branches together, or one branch at a time. The Professional plan allows up to 5 branches. Enterprise has no limit."
---
{#- ── Hero ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -#}
